cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CFFM-Net: Reliability-Gated Selective State-Space Fusion of Visible and Thermal Cameras for Small-Object Detection"
authors:
  - family-names: Roshan
    given-names: Ritesh
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/riteshroshann/yolo-cross-feature-fusion-mamba-net"
keywords:
  - object detection
  - visible-thermal fusion
  - multispectral
  - state space models
  - Mamba
  - YOLO26
  - small objects
  - sensor reliability
abstract: >-
  CFFM-Net fuses a visible and a thermal camera for small-object detection. Two YOLO26 backbones are fused at four
  pyramid levels by a selective state-space scan over interleaved visible and thermal tokens, in which the
  discretisation step of every token is scaled by a learned per-pixel estimate of its camera's reliability, so that
  tokens from an unreliable or failed camera are skipped by construction.
